"JH" <no@email> writes:
> I saw a shimmering dragon that was commented out in monst.c.  Sounds
> interesting, so I was thinking about uncomment it.  Does anyone here know if
> that's the only thing I would need to uncomment, or do I also have to change
> settings elsewhere?

There's a few other references you'd need to uncomment back in to make
the scales work and babies grow up properly:

mon.c-#if 0     /* DEFERRED */
mon.c:      case PM_SHIMMERING_DRAGON:
mon.c-#endif
--
mondata.c-#if 0 /* DEFERRED */
mondata.c:      {PM_BABY_SHIMMERING_DRAGON, PM_SHIMMERING_DRAGON},
mondata.c-#endif
--
objects.c-#if 0 /* DEFERRED */
objects.c:DRGN_ARMR("shimmering dragon scale mail", 1, DISPLACED, 1200, 1, CLR_CYAN),
objects.c-#endif
--
objects.c-#if 0 /* DEFERRED */
objects.c:DRGN_ARMR("shimmering dragon scales", 0, DISPLACED,  700, 7, CLR_CYAN),
objects.c-#endif
--
polyself.c-#if 0        /* DEFERRED */
polyself.c:         case SHIMMERING_DRAGON_SCALE_MAIL:
polyself.c:         case SHIMMERING_DRAGON_SCALES:
polyself.c:             return PM_SHIMMERING_DRAGON;
polyself.c-#endif

and you'll want to comment out the tile substitutions in
win/share/tilemap.c.

> (has anyone patched this already, i.e. am I re-inventing the wheel?)

Well, the dragon in question is present in SLASH'EM; my hypothesis for
its being commented out in vanilla is that the DevTeam are waiting on
implementing monster displacement, so you don't get the advantage of
the scales' property without the disadvantage of the dragon's
property.

